# Cooker UAT environment file
#
# Copy this to `.env.uat` (gitignored) before running `make uat-up`,
# then fill in the values for the OIDC provider you want to test with.
#
#     cp .env.uat.example .env.uat
#     $EDITOR .env.uat
#     make uat-up
#
# Leaving COOKER_OIDC_ENABLED unset (or false) keeps the dev admin
# user behaviour: any unauthenticated request to /api/v1 is treated
# as the seed admin. Useful for smoke-testing pipelines without an
# IdP.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: COOKER_SECRET_KEY is auto-appended by `make uat-up` so
# you don't need to set it here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime tunables (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# COOKER_ORPHAN_SWEEP_INTERVAL controls the staleness window the
# boot-time orphan sweep uses to mark in-flight pipeline_runs rows
# as `failed` after a crash. Go duration string. Default 60s.
# Must be > 30s (heartbeatInterval) — values <= 30s are ignored and
# the default is used so the sweep can't reap healthy runs that
# happened to miss a single heartbeat tick.
#
#COOKER_ORPHAN_SWEEP_INTERVAL=60s

# COOKER_EDGE_CONDITIONS_ENABLED gates edge-condition evaluation
# (success/failure/always trajectories + the skipped stage status +
# continue-through-failure runs). Default true; set false to restore
# the legacy all-success/abort-on-first-failure behaviour.
#
#COOKER_EDGE_CONDITIONS_ENABLED=true

# COOKER_BUILD_CACHE_REPO, when set, stamps a registry layer-cache
# ref onto the build stages of app-deploy synthesized pipelines
# (Kaniko --cache-repo / Buildah --cache-to / BuildKit cache
# exports). The builder's credentials must allow pushing to it.
# Hand-built pipelines configure cache per stage in the editor.
# See docs/build-cache.md.
#
#COOKER_BUILD_CACHE_REPO=registry.example.com/cooker/buildcache

# AI failure triage (roadmap M4) — opt-in. When enabled, clicking
# "Why did this fail?" on a failed stage sends that stage's sanitized
# config summary, error and the LAST 32 KiB OF ITS LOGS to the
# Anthropic API (data egress!). Secrets are stripped (env values and
# secretRefs never travel); the API key stays server-side. The
# response is advisory text only — Cooker never acts on it.
#
#COOKER_AI_TRIAGE_ENABLED=true
#COOKER_AI_TRIAGE_MODEL=claude-fable-5
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Audit trail. COOKER_AUDIT_DESTINATION takes a comma list of sinks:
#   stdout — JSON via slog (default); ship with the cluster log stack
#   file   — append-only JSON Lines at COOKER_AUDIT_FILE_PATH (SIEM
#            tail-shipping; no query path)
#   db     — async insert into the audit_events table; queryable at
#            GET /api/v1/admin/audit and the /admin/audit UI. Writer
#            is drop-on-full: a down Postgres loses events, never
#            blocks requests — pair with stdout/file for a
#            loss-resistant copy. Rows older than
#            COOKER_AUDIT_DB_RETENTION are swept daily (default
#            2160h = 90 days; 0 disables). Production requires
#            DATABASE_URL when db is selected.
#
#COOKER_AUDIT_ENABLED=true
#COOKER_AUDIT_DESTINATION=db,stdout
#COOKER_AUDIT_DB_RETENTION=2160h

#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# OIDC — pick ONE provider section below, uncomment, fill in values
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Backend
#COOKER_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#COOKER_OIDC_ISSUER_URL=
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
#COOKER_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:8080/callback
#COOKER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Local email + password auth (homelab / single-user fallback)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables POST /api/v1/auth/local/{signup,signin,me} alongside the
# OIDC path. Both can be active at the same time. The first signup is
# auto-promoted to admin; subsequent signups default to viewer.
# See SECURITY.md for the trade-offs (no MFA, no password reset, no
# revocation list — this is intentionally minimal).
#
# JWT_SIGNING_KEY: base64 (preferred, matches COOKER_SECRET_KEY) or
# raw bytes; must decode to >= 32 bytes. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
#COOKER_LOCAL_AUTH_ENABLED=true
#COOKER_LOCAL_AUTH_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=CHANGE_ME_BASE64_32_BYTES
#COOKER_LOCAL_AUTH_TOKEN_TTL=12h
#COOKER_LOCAL_AUTH_ALLOW_SIGNUP=true

# Frontend (baked into the JS bundle at build time — must match backend)
#VITE_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=
#VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
#VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080/callback
#VITE_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080
#VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email groups


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider preset: Google
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Visit https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# 2. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID, type = "Web application"
# 3. Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:8080/callback
# 4. Copy the Client ID below; the client secret is NOT required
#    (the browser uses PKCE, no secret needed).
# 5. Note: Google does not emit a `groups` claim by default. Without
#    Google Workspace + custom claims, all users will fall back to
#    the "viewer" role per backend/internal/auth/rbac.go:95.
#    For full RBAC testing, prefer KeepSave or Keycloak.
#
#COOKER_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#COOKER_OIDC_ISSUER_URL=https://accounts.google.com
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
#COOKER_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:8080/callback
#COOKER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080
#VITE_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://accounts.google.com
#VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
#VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080/callback
#VITE_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080
#VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider preset: Keycloak (`make uat-up-with-keycloak`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# `make uat-up-with-keycloak` boots a Keycloak container alongside
# Cooker and pre-seeds a realm with two users (alice/alice = admin,
# bob/bob = viewer). The Makefile target appends these values to
# .env.uat for you; this preset is documented here so operators
# can inspect what's wired without running the target.
#
# Linux operators (no Docker Desktop) must one-time add to /etc/hosts:
#   127.0.0.1 host.docker.internal
#
#COOKER_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#COOKER_OIDC_ISSUER_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8081/realms/cooker
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=cooker
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
#COOKER_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:8080/callback
#COOKER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080
#VITE_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=http://host.docker.internal:8081/realms/cooker
#VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=cooker
#VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080/callback
#VITE_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080
#VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email groups


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider preset: KeepSave (custom OIDC IdP)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Replace https://keepsave.example.com with your KeepSave instance.
# KeepSave must expose the OIDC discovery document at
#   <issuer>/.well-known/openid-configuration
# and the token must include a `groups` (or `roles`) claim with one
# of: cooker-admins, cooker-operators, cooker-approvers,
# cooker-viewers — see backend/internal/auth/rbac.go:77 for the
# group-to-role mapping.
#
#COOKER_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#COOKER_OIDC_ISSUER_URL=https://keepsave.example.com
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=cooker
#COOKER_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
#COOKER_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:8080/callback
#COOKER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080
#VITE_OIDC_ENABLED=true
#VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://keepsave.example.com
#VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=cooker
#VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080/callback
#VITE_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8080
#VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email groups
